Publish IOBSD before the matching starts

Two personalities on this board ask for the IOBSD resource:

    'IOClass'         = NativeAES;
    'IOProviderClass' = IOResources;
    'IOResourceMatch' = IOBSD;

    'IOClass'         = NativeRamBlock;
    'IOProviderClass' = IOResources;
    'IOResourceMatch' = IOBSD;

A driver that asks for a resource waits for it in startCandidate(), and
that wait is the "nio: WAIT IOBSD" line on the panel.  The resource is
published by IOKitBSDInit(), which bsd_init() calls -- and bsd_init() runs
at waypoint 9, after the matching, which runs at waypoint 6.  So the two
wait for each other: the matching waits for a resource that only comes
after the matching, and the boot never gets past it.  The photographs of
every round since 549 show that wait, and the board stops there.

The resource does not have to mean what it means on a Mac.  It says that the
BSD side of IOKit is up.  This board's root filesystem is not on a BSD
volume at all: it is the mockfs image in RAM that the loader puts into the
device tree, and the rootfs.img in it carries the real launchd and the real
dyld.  Nothing on the path to the userland needs the storage driver to
bring a real BSD volume up, and the storage driver on this board never
publishes the resource anyway -- it matches for observation only and does
not touch the controller.

So the resource is published here, before the matching, and the two
personalities that wait for it walk straight past it.  The wait ends
immediately, because checkResource() looks the resource up first and
returns as soon as it is there.  It is published again by IOKitBSDInit()
when bsd_init() runs, which is the genuine publication and the one that
matters; this one only lets the matching finish.

The line on the panel says the resource was published, and that it was
published early, so a photograph says which boot published it.

